dictions on Test Images","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Ynfac5F8uL"}],"identifier":"visualizing-predictions-on-test-images","label":"Visualizing Predictions on Test Images","html_id":"visualizing-predictions-on-test-images","implicit":true,"key":"Z02Ot6zP3h"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"After training finishes, this cell loads the best checkpoint and runs inference on every image in the test split. For each image, it does two things. First, it calls the YOLO model and saves annotated output images (with masks and bounding boxes drawn) to ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"BGAOsQRykS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/content/runs/segment/predict","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"KsbbteMXWL"},{"type":"text","value":". Second, it computes a simple coverage statistic: all instance masks are merged into a single binary mask, and the fraction of the image that mask covers is reported as a percentage.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Jlvh68Sph8"}],"key":"U8mRYeoXRz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"That coverage number is not a biological measurement on its own, but it is a useful sanity check. If you are segmenting a reef transect image and the model reports 0.3% coverage, something has almost certainly gone wrong (either no detections or very tight masks). If it reports 85% coverage on an image that is mostly open water, the masks are probably overflowing their targets. Use the Plotly figure titles to scan quickly before doing any deeper analysis.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"O2iAZakntb"}],"key":"h4JviqrU4Z"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"fJrL8v3dIQ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"px.imshow","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"Qoc10f25Go"},{"type":"text","value":" call renders each annotated image as an interactive Plotly figure. You can zoom in to inspect mask boundaries, which is especially useful for evaluating whether the model cleanly separates adjacent coral colonies or fish that are partially occluding one another.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"Zmc6UwXkzz"}],"key":"NuCYTJwtXU"}],"key":"RPBuCGWnDx"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"id":"7k5ReJusOBxG","outputId":"a9d89859-6861-45c5-bce7-bf7fc64b123c","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# Set Plotly to use the Colab renderer\npio.renderers.default = \"colab\"\n\n# Directories\ntest_image_dir = \"/content/dataset/test/images\"\nsaved_output_dir = \"/content/runs/segment/predict\"\n\nmodel = YOLO(\"/content/runs/segment/train/weights/best.pt\")\n\nresults = model(test_image_dir, save=True)\n\n# Iterate over the results for each image processed\nfor result in results:\n    orig_path = result.path  # the path of the input image\n    base_name = os.path.basename(orig_path)\n        orig_img = cv2.imread(orig_path)\n    if orig_img is None:\n        print(f\"Could not load image {orig_path}. Skipping.\")\n        continue\n    orig_img = cv2.cvtColor(orig_img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n    h, w = orig_img.shape[:2]\n    total_pixels = h * w\n\n    mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=np.uint8)\n\n    # If any segmentation masks were returned, combine them.\n    if result.masks is not None and result.masks.data is not None:\n        for m in result.masks.data:\n            m_np = m.cpu().numpy() if hasattr(m, \"cpu\") else m\n            m_bin = (m_np > 0.5).astype(np.uint8)\n            mask = np.maximum(mask, m_bin)\n\n    # Calculate the number of pixels in the mask and its percentage coverage over the image.\n    mask_pixel_count = int(np.sum(mask))\n    coverage = (mask_pixel_count / total_pixels) * 100\n\n    saved_img_path = os.path.join(saved_output_dir, base_name)\n    if not os.path.exists(saved_img_path):\n        print(f\"Saved image for {base_name} not found in {saved_output_dir}.\")\n        continue\n\n    saved_img = cv2.imread(saved_img_path)\n    saved_img = cv2.cvtColor(saved_img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n\n    fig = px.imshow(saved_img, title=f\"{base_name}: {coverage:.2f}% coverage, {mask_pixel_count} pixels\")\n    fig.update_xaxes(showticklabels=False)\n    fig.update_yaxes(showticklabels=False)\n    fig.show()\n","key":"MntrNpzGWI"},{"type":"outputs","id":"pd_npfvSa6sclAwhHLdgb","children":[{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":"\nimage 1/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230704_174611_mp4-8_jpg.rf.e616459a2ba009da3e97af91ee6896e9.jpg: 640x640 1 phaceolid, 12.0ms\nimage 2/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_123255_jpg.rf.83ef6c419fb9450cc30533be3a0f3152.jpg: 640x640 1 Parascolymia, 10.8ms\nimage 3/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_123544_jpg.rf.68e223d29096ccf784464c9d4e08160f.jpg: 640x640 1 Parascolymia, 11.1ms\nimage 4/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_123650_jpg.rf.4e4157deb8ec4d1e4574e9414e8f10ce.jpg: 640x640 1 Parascolymia, 10.8ms\nimage 5/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_124126_jpg.rf.8e7d988292723a46eb3283dca055a962.jpg: 640x640 1 phaceolid, 10.8ms\nimage 6/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_124409_jpg.rf.871e34845775219697ebe21e97cb13c3.jpg: 640x640 1 phaceolid, 10.7ms\nimage 7/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_124510_jpg.rf.10f413fa7f82a5196905071454271061.jpg: 640x640 1 phaceolid, 11.0ms\nimage 8/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_124619_jpg.rf.f539c120bb7a0c8568a490654b824394.jpg: 640x640 1 massive, 11.5ms\nimage 9/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_124712_jpg.rf.cbcb6be5d2e9999b1aad9cd87fc43f11.jpg: 640x640 1 massive, 11.9ms\nimage 10/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_124915_jpg.rf.7df15bfc9f192d8bf1811121154b0871.jpg: 640x640 1 submassive, 11.4ms\nimage 11/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_125036_jpg.rf.fc23a71e88b2f989140870a79a9c2ea3.jpg: 640x640 1 Encrusting, 1 branching, 11.1ms\nimage 12/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_125447_jpg.rf.7f40cac22f123bca6e074adc2c4f7a19.jpg: 640x640 1 branching, 11.2ms\nimage 13/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_130442_jpg.rf.e8a337d3a2f754e0862ac1dd807302c4.jpg: 640x640 1 submassive, 11.0ms\nimage 14/14 /content/dataset/test/images/20230829_130539_jpg.rf.1b6b1a3dceee3da29739ade4bcca6969.jpg: 640x640 2 branchings, 11.2ms\nSpeed: 2.3ms preprocess, 11.2ms inference, 1.9ms postprocess per image at shape (1, 3, 640, 640)\nResults saved to \u001b[1mruns/segment/predict3\u001b[0m\n"},"children":[],"key":"bnjqf3GZM6"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"bd9919489d8ec2c91c29010c74e36e29","path":"/build/bd9919489d8ec2c91c29010c74e36e29.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"L3BXnSwOWF"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"95f07991b6120f289d59daaaef33d5ff","path":"/build/95f07991b6120f289d59daaaef33d5ff.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"hS1tZDjY38"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"96730f9d5c672a3774146343ba8ae4d1","path":"/build/96730f9d5c672a3774146343ba8ae4d1.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"db2DbGIlxD"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"e56c804afcd0a6a49cef8a41ff173e01","path":"/build/e56c804afcd0a6a49cef8a41ff173e01.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"miRKDDo3yZ"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"4813de0a23ce1a55c4d14f6787828b22","path":"/build/4813de0a23ce1a55c4d14f6787828b22.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"UrVI6BftQS"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"86492db01485407f4fe7662ce85f040c","path":"/build/86492db01485407f4fe7662ce85f040c.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"miehjVtWp8"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"4576c31dc2269122fdf94f24c0c88325","path":"/build/4576c31dc2269122fdf94f24c0c88325.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"Cac15WkQxL"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"48d036848cc5ea77192d8db1faa78e0f","path":"/build/48d036848cc5ea77192d8db1faa78e0f.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"ArCyoYuLzm"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"a4d2786ee5153429b315834732bb60e3","path":"/build/a4d2786ee5153429b315834732bb60e3.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"vH8YdAI9G7"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"b2fb42be859fd2b150975bd0983c5078","path":"/build/b2fb42be859fd2b150975bd0983c5078.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"MDhvWP2oGd"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"bcf430617bf8ad69668dd0145c9b0004","path":"/build/bcf430617bf8ad69668dd0145c9b0004.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"J1RAO8VvNS"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"34ae11874c8992172a95ad24370b6b6a","path":"/build/34ae11874c8992172a95ad24370b6b6a.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"iw9YP0MFwo"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"df5309a784f0c2573901cdcdc269ade7","path":"/build/df5309a784f0c2573901cdcdc269ade7.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"uREozXuQFW"},{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"output_type":"display_data","metadata":{},"data":{"text/html":{"content_type":"text/html","hash":"c5ea30a4a34b1455692f9f4f868d5a44","path":"/build/c5ea30a4a34b1455692f9f4f868d5a44.html"}}},"children":[],"key":"eDOMl1Vi8l"}],"key":"wZARvR6b0m"}],"key":"L917WIMjyw"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","data":{"id":"NhIwwxboOBRg"},"children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reflecting on Results","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"bSVBmuhafh"}],"identifier":"reflecting-on-results","label":"Reflecting on Results","html_id":"reflecting-on-results","implicit":true,"key":"rJ5idbB11l"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instance segmentation produces a polygon mask for each detected object rather than a simple rectangular boundary. This extra precision matters for downstream analysis: you can count individuals, measure each organism’s pixel area, and track specific animals across frames without conflating overlapping neighbors. Bounding boxes tell you where something is; masks tell you exactly which pixels belong to it, which is the foundation for any morphometric or density estimate you want to extract automatically.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"z1tx0eULJ7"}],"key":"OZEjjydtyQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spend some time reviewing the outputs from the final visualization cell. Check whether the masks follow the actual body outline of each organism or whether they collapse into rough approximations that miss fins, tails, or protruding features. Pay particular attention to crowded frames where two animals overlap: note whether the model correctly separates their masks or whether one mask bleeds into the adjacent object.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"gRUtZkBZx4"}],"key":"VIrY3ji90b"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reflection questions:","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"bZInCTkhx2"}],"key":"XRlxJbr724"}],"key":"n6X32RVuk5"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How does an instance segmentation mask differ from a simple bounding box in terms of information content, and what analyses become possible once you have per-pixel labels?","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"SU6qxNeAzU"}],"key":"NpxjQcOBeM"}],"key":"mM3TVM49Zk"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For your marine dataset, which species or object types are most difficult to segment cleanly, and why (consider body shape, coloration, motion blur, or density of individuals)?","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"AbzllgNDzZ"}],"key":"T0BoLeZoBd"}],"key":"yYB0qHHZ1h"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How might you use mask area (measured in pixels and converted to real-world units via camera calibration) as a proxy for biomass or organism size, and what sources of error would you need to account for?","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"zm2kucsqqo"}],"key":"v2B44kD5zx"}],"key":"pUAWlxPlyn"}],"key":"DuHs5BwSrq"}],"key":"hoiMPF8C73"}],"key":"O50vFnoYfU"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"3.9 Keypoint Detection With YOLO","url":"/book/keypoint-yolo","group":"Chapter 3 - Computer Vision Development"},"next":{"title":"Restarting YOLO","url":"/book/restarting-yolo","group":"Chapter 3 - Computer Vision Development"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}